  "decision": {
    "next_work_package_proposal": "WP-MTP-COMPACT-FP8-TABLE-20261014 / AC-MTP-GREEDY-v83",
    "mechanism": "Store FP8 codebook values exactly as BF16 with32lane replicas (16KiB total). A32bit bank word holds paired lane replicas; expand the16bit word to identical FP32 only at consumption. Publish with four warp-broadcast/128bit-store rounds, replacing the old32-round scalar publication. Preserve packed global feed, all FMA chains, reduction and output boundaries. Explicit shared carveout must preserve available residency.",
    "why_new": "The closed32KiB FP32 lane-table construction used32shuffle/store publication rounds. This representation halves shared storage and publication bytes with a different subword consumer; it is not a scan of replica count or a revival of that exact implementation. Measured excess shared wavefronts now supplies causal motivation, not a speedup guarantee.",
    "contract": "All256code values including signed zero/canonical quiet NaN roundtrip bitwise. Host address proof covers1,048,576code-pair cases, <=2distinct words per bank and exact unique publication of8192cells. New device/SASS/resources and full output/state admission remain required.",
    "composition_boundary": "One compact-table implementation, no alternate layouts or parameters. Complete M2/3/4 canonical/sidecar special-code outputs and P65 full prefix state, then immediate d2 API; useful long direction unlocks d3. No further profiler in this work package.",
    "limits": [
      "BF16 storage does not relax target precision: operands must expand to exactly original FP32 bits.",
      "More shared storage than current1KiB table and extra expansion instructions can offset reduced conflicts.",
      "NCU heuristic57.58%local-speedup and occupancy hint50% are not forecasts; never add or present as project performance.",
      "No DRAM-bandwidth or whole-model hardware-ceiling conclusion. One median layer and deterministic activations do not cover all production roles."
    ]
  },
